CODEGEN.md §2.11, §3.5, DECISIONS 435: a Decode<N> part is a member of detail::AAccess and names the namespace function LoadModeFromWire (the enum LoadMode's FromWire) unqualified; the loader of the value modeFromWire has that name, so inside the access struct it hides the function (g++: "no matching function for call to Decoder::Enum") whatever Potion's width and whether or not its Decode is cut. Every namespace name an access member equals collides, not only the types a decoder names.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// Named so that its FromWire is the loader of the value modeFromWire.
enum LoadMode { alpha, beta }

/// A potion.
record Potion {
  /// Its key.
  name: String
  /// Its mode.
  mode: LoadMode
}

/// The potions.
let potions: [Potion] keyed by name = [{ name: "a", mode: LoadMode.alpha }]

/// Named like the FromWire of LoadMode, behind Load.
let modeFromWire: [Potion] keyed by name = [{ name: "b", mode: LoadMode.beta }]

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "a", mode: data }
emit json { out: "out/" }
-- a.potions.json --
[{ "name": "a", "mode": "alpha" }]
-- a.modeFromWire.json --
[{ "name": "b", "mode": "beta" }]
